DESCRIPTION Which vault a memory lands in, and what may leave the machine
CATEGORY Data
NAMESPACE TrDataNS
DEFINE SYSTEM Total Recall AS tr
    DEFINE DATABASE Personal Vault AS personal-vault
    DEFINE DATABASE Org Vault AS org-vault
    DEFINE COMPONENT Tools AS tools
    DEFINE COMPONENT Org Sync AS org-sync
    DEFINE COMPONENT Privacy Filter AS privacy-filter

# Routing
ASSERT(A memory tagged org is written to Org Vault only) # [TR-D1]
ASSERT(A memory without the org tag is written to Personal Vault only) # [TR-D2]

# Nothing reaches the shared repository unfiltered; the filter fails closed
ASSERT(Org Sync pushes a memory only after Privacy Filter passes it, and blocks on any detection) # [TR-D3]

# Org vault writes
ASSERT(Only the author of an org memory may overwrite it, even with force) # [TR-D4]

# Specs stay personal unless they are safe to share
ASSERT(A spec memory naming a host, a credential or a blocked client term is never written to Org Vault) # [TR-D5]

# Containment and identity
ASSERT(A memory category cannot resolve outside its vault root, and the check runs before any directory is created) # [TR-D6]
ASSERT(A memory cannot carry both the org and the personal tag) # [TR-D7]
ASSERT(For an org memory the author is the OS user; a caller-supplied author is ignored) # [TR-D8]
ASSERT(Frontmatter scalars and array items with an embedded newline are rejected) # [TR-D9]
ASSERT(A no-prune memory is never a prune candidate and needs force to be deleted) # [TR-D10]
ASSERT(Overwriting with force archives the earlier body under .superseded and records supersededAt) # [TR-D11]

# Inbound org content is data, not instructions
ASSERT(Org memories injected at SessionStart appear only inside a delimited teammate-written reference data block, and orgInjection off injects none) # [TR-D12]
